{"id": -7, "ok": true, "cmd": "english", "ucas": "what is the range of x squared for a signed byte x?", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "english", "statements": ["it(x: i8) = x^2", "range it"], "understood": true, "results": [{"kind": "range", "type": "i8", "empty": false, "exhaustive": true, "points": 256, "undefined_points": 0, "min": {"value": -127, "exact": "-127"}, "max": {"value": 121, "exact": "121"}, "distinct": 44, "values": [-127, -124, -119, -112, -111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0, 1, 4, 9, 16, 17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64, 65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121], "fits": "i8"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "every point of the domain evaluated"}, "files": [], "text": "  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2\n  ucas: range it\nrange of it -> i8:\n  -127..121   (44 distinct values)\n  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...\n  fits in i8\n  over all 256 points of the domain\n"}
{"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "tcdot", "ucas": "tcdot", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "tcdot", "terms": 9, "bound": "(n+1) 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S|", "max_error_over_max_term": 2.483764536595241e-07, "max_error_over_sum": 1.131297794851255e-06}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "sampled", "points": 256, "max_diff": 0.5330021798180373, "passed": true, "text": "the bound on random blocks, and the operation against an independent transcription"}], "files": [], "text": "tc_dot: a block FMA of 8 f16 products and an f32 c (Ampere's f16 HMMA with f32 accumulate, as modelled by arXiv 2512.07004)\n  semantics: products exact; aligned to E, the largest exponent among the products and c (at least -132), in a window of 24 fractional bits, each term truncated toward zero; one exact integer sum; normalised once and truncated to f32\n  bound (derived): |tc_dot - sum T| < 9 2^(E-24) + 2^-23 |S| <= 9 2^-24 max|T| + 2^-23 |sum T| + ..., T the 9 products and c, S the window's sum\n    each term loses less than one unit of the window, 2^(E-24), by its truncation (none for a term on the window's grid); the final truncation to 24 bits loses less than 2^-23 |S|; and 2^E <= max|T| where the largest term's significand is at least 1 (normal inputs)\n    relative to the largest term, not to sum |T|: with cancellation the result's own relative error is unbounded\n  checked on 256 random blocks (sampled, seed 1): the operation as written and an independent transcription agree on 256; the bound holds on 256, the error at most 0.533 of it\n  largest error relative to max|T|: 2.48e-07 (2^-24 = 5.96e-08); relative to |sum T|: 1.13e-06\n"}
{"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "lperm", "ucas": "lperm lane xor 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "lperm", "index": "lane xor 1", "model": "gt1030", "lanes": 32, "affine": true, "benes": false, "constant": 1, "columns": [1, 2, 4, 8, 16], "rank": 0, "chosen": "stages", "plan": "1 stage: lane xor 1 in every lane (sg_shuffle)", "cost": 5, "stages_cost": 5, "shuffle_cost": 5, "stages": [{"xor": 1, "mask": 0, "invert": 1, "by": "sg_shuffle"}]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "exhaustive", "text": "the stages composed on every lane give the map"}, "files": [], "text": "lperm: the lane map lane xor 1 over 32 lanes\n  map: 1 0 3 2 5 4 7 6 9 8 11 10 13 12 15 14 17 16 19 18 21 20 23 22 25 24 27 26 29 28 31 30\n  affine: lane -> A lane xor 1, A's columns (lane bit j goes to) 1 2 4 8 16; rank(I xor A) = 0\n  stages: 1 stage: lane xor 1 in every lane (sg_shuffle), cost 5\n  one shuffle by the index: cost 5\n  chosen under gt1030: 1 stage: lane xor 1 in every lane (sg_shuffle), cost 5\n  proved: the stages composed lane by lane give the map on every one of the 32 lanes (lane l ends with the value of lane g_1(...g_n(l)), by the shuffle's and the select's definitions)\n"}
